model_guard.py --depth 5 on the round-22 Policy: NOT COMPLETED.
The round-22 model adds a session-less agent (BOT3), session s5, a forceGuarded toggle and unguard moves,
which grows depth 5 roughly 25x over round 16's 5.2M transitions. The content-deduplicated seen set holds a
JSON copy of every state, so the run reached ~80 GB of committed memory without finishing and was stopped.
Evidence for round 22 is the depth-4 run (933,044 transitions, all six properties hold, 35/35 mutations caught;
see ref/RESULTS.md). Running depth 5 needs a leaner state encoding (e.g. hashing states) and a memory cap.
